00:28:21,773 --> 00:28:21,980
I don't know.

276
00:28:22,210 --> 00:28:28,710
[her voice] Lauren.

277
00:28:33,270 --> 00:28:41,650
[her voice] I'm going to say something, and it's going to be unkind, and I'm sorry, and I'd do it again.

278
00:28:42,180 --> 00:28:47,740
[her voice] Count backwards for me. I'll be here at one.

279
00:29:08,270 --> 00:29:10,070
My mother said that.

280
00:29:10,150 --> 00:29:11,198
Lauren-

281
00:29:11,278 --> 00:29:16,650
My mother said that to me. Every night. Nobody knows that.

282
00:29:17,270 --> 00:29:25,650
I have never said that out loud. Not once. Not here. Not to him.

283
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:28,814
[her voice] I know.

284
00:29:28,894 --> 00:29:33,680
[her voice] She said it to me too.

285
00:29:34,210 --> 00:29:40,710
[her voice] Didn't she, [ - - - ]

286
00:29:41,210 --> 00:29:47,710
What did you just call her.

287
00:29:55,210 --> 00:29:57,677
What am I?

288
00:29:57,757 --> 00:30:01,710
[her voice] You're the one who-

289
00:31:35,240 --> 00:31:36,160
Back door.

290
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:37,160
No.

291
00:31:37,240 --> 00:31:40,997
Lauren, the alley's clear, you go left and you're-

292
00:31:41,077 --> 00:31:41,997
No.

293
00:31:42,077 --> 00:31:42,980
Please.

294
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:50,680
I'm not doing the part where you decide for me twice in one night.

295
00:31:51,270 --> 00:31:52,801
That's not what this is.

296
00:31:52,881 --> 00:31:54,681
That's exactly what this is.

297
00:31:54,761 --> 00:31:59,650
You've done it for six years. It's the only thing you're actually good at.

298
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:07,680
Miles. We're doing this one together or we're not doing it.

299
00:32:08,180 --> 00:32:10,920
Okay.

300
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:13,740
Okay.

301
00:32:21,210 --> 00:32:26,257
There's something you need to know before that gets to zero.

302
00:32:26,337 --> 00:32:27,710
Then say it fast.

303
00:32:28,270 --> 00:32:29,683
Nobody comes over.

304
00:32:29,763 --> 00:32:30,683
What?

305
00:32:30,763 --> 00:32:36,655
It's not against the rules. It's - Lauren, it isn't a rule, it's a fact.

306
00:32:37,300 --> 00:32:40,436
People don't cross. Things don't cross.

307
00:32:40,516 --> 00:32:41,436
We crossed.

308
00:32:41,516 --> 00:32:46,631
We came out. That's different. That's falling. Anyone can fall.

309
00:32:47,270 --> 00:32:52,166
Coming the other way costs something. It costs more than a person has.

310
00:32:52,246 --> 00:32:53,166
Meaning what.

311
00:32:53,246 --> 00:32:55,726
Meaning nothing comes through whole.

312
00:32:56,300 --> 00:33:02,466
So whatever is out there - whatever it used to be - it paid everything it had to stand on our step.

313
00:33:02,546 --> 00:33:05,620
And it did that on purpose. And it did it tonight.

314
00:33:10,270 --> 00:33:17,365
Miles, I have to ask you something and I need you to not manage me.

315
00:33:17,445 --> 00:33:18,650
Okay.

316
00:33:19,210 --> 00:33:21,722
That message.

317
00:33:21,802 --> 00:33:25,710
Did it come from me?

318
00:33:37,150 --> 00:33:41,770
Okay.

319
00:33:57,120 --> 00:34:00,800
Who are you?

320
00:34:01,300 --> 00:34:08,531
[her voice] I'm the one who left when they told me to.

321
00:34:08,611 --> 00:34:10,620
[her voice] Don't.

322
00:34:40,210 --> 00:34:43,420
Miles.

323
00:34:43,500 --> 00:34:46,710
Miles, what.

324
00:34:47,180 --> 00:34:52,740
[muffled, through the door] It's me.

325
00:36:03,150 --> 00:36:07,770
[SYSTEM VOICE] Retrieval is already in progress.

